774	     * {@link #identityKey(Owner) identityKey} exactly equals that of an existing, non-deleted owner.
775	     * Because the key is the SHA-256 of the normalized telephone, lower-cased email and
776	     * {@code soundex(lastName)} joined together, this one check is the sole duplicate rule: only an
777	     * exact full-key match counts as a duplicate, so two owners sharing a lastName and postcode but
778	     * carrying different telephones have different keys and are both allowed (the second is instead
779	     * flagged a soft match).
